;; Hand-maintained cljfmt :indents for the body-macros this artifact uses.
;;
;; Only genuine macros belong here. `with-dump-file` and `with-assertions` read
;; like binders and are plain functions taking a callback, so cljfmt's default
;; call alignment is the correct one for them — an entry would misindent every
;; call site. The test one is local; `with-deferred-settle` is core's, which is
;; why a harvester run in this tree cannot see its :style/indent the way core's
;; own run does.
;;
;; project.clj splices this into the :cljfmt :extra-indents, appended onto
;; cljfmt's defaults (which its :indents would otherwise replace). Match is by
;; bare macro name, regardless of ns alias — `v/with-deferred-settle` included.
{with-deferred-settle [[:block 1]]
 with-cleared-kb      [[:block 1]]}
